==English==

===Etymology===
Norman baronial surname from a place ''Perci'' in Normandy, Late Latin ''Persiacum'', from the Gallo-Roman personal name ''[[Persius]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɜː(r)si|-ɜː(r)si]]

===Proper noun===
'''Percy'''
# An [[English]] [[surname]].
# {{given name|male}}, transferred use of the surname since the Middle Ages, also used as a pet form of [[Piers]] and [[Percival]].

